The original constructor first default-constructs `values` and `stringIndexes` and then copy-assigns them. Copy-constructing them directly in the member initializer list skips that wasted default-construction step. The result is identical, and any other members are still default-initialized as before.

```cpp
FieldBase::FieldBase(const FieldBase &field)
    : values(field.values), stringIndexes(field.stringIndexes)
{
}
```